  "note": "Read the accuracy, mean-confidence, separation and AUROC columns together, and do not reduce the interpretation to the two aggregate columns. Several patterns are possible and each means something different: accuracy falling while mean confidence stays flat means the model does not register the degradation; accuracy and confidence falling together means it partly does; a falling AUROC with flat mean confidence means the correct and wrong distributions are converging, so confidence is becoming a worse error signal regardless of its average. The no_retrieval condition uses no documents, so it is identical at every k by construction and acts as the flat control.",
